# V7c: the matmul sweep with the model cache pointed at the rig cache (V7b defaulted to the runner home).
# V7: the MLP gate and up 64-row matmul sweep at the FOUR-CARD per-chip shapes (K = 5,120, N = 4,352 = 136 tiles, bfloat4_b as served), on card
# M alone, eager (matmul_tp4_sweep.py, harness optimisation/ttnn-op/matmul_tp4_sweep/run_card_m.sh). The TP2 sweep (matmul64_sweep.py) has
# MODEL_TP = 2; at four cards the builder puts the gate on 68 cores (per_core_N 2) and the up on 34 (per_core_N 4), and the profile has the
# gate 8.8 us per call SLOWER than the up with twice the cores. Stage 1: every per_core_N that fits the 11 x 10 worker grid on the model's grid
# width and block; stage 2: the best four per_core_N over grid width (8, 10, 11), in0_block_w and the output subblock. Every config's output is
# compared byte for byte with the model's current config on the same inputs; the answer is the best EXACT config.
# One card: the cardm step runs card M only and needs no reset before it (A0 freed the cards); after it the next job resets all four.
# Duration (estimate): 30-45 min (about 230 configs per shape compile once each; container timeout 40 min).
# Read: report tp4sweep-<stamp>.json in the cardm results and the TP4_SWEEP lines: per shape the current config and time, the best exact
# config and time, the speed-up, the DRAM floor (gate 31 us, 58% of 405 GB/s measured today) and the tp_common builder arguments
# (num_cores, grid_w) that reproduce the best partition. Pass: passed=true, a best_exact for gate and up. NOTHING IS APPLIED by this job: the
# result is the input of a graft change (the T1-style hook in the model config) that is a later lane's.
# OPTIONAL: its product is data; a failure or a hang (the harness prints the reset line) does not stop the window, and the next job resets.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/next-3-cheap window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-3-cheap and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The window's jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed
# from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image a build-only job builds from this same commit while production serves (it
# carries draft_wide_tp, which is new); a later commit needs a new tag. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3a is a PLACEHOLDER: the driver of the window
# may substitute it (in every template) once the image is built from the pushed branch.
# PRODUCTION IS LIVE ON THE CARDS when the window opens: A0 is the first job and the only one that takes it down.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3a
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/matmul_tp4_sweep/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--shapes mlp_w1,mlp_w3
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-3a HF_CACHE=/home/thatch/hf-cache
